From 44d2d1644514159bf68007c1683c61505493b2f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Suiche <msuiche@enidon.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 19:48:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 258/259] DeepSeek-V4.1: GLP steering at the folded post-layer
 residual, off unless WEIGHTLESS_STEER_PATH is set

A weightless GLP file (github.com/msuiche/weightless, docs/spec/GLP.md)
projects one unit direction per layer off the residual stream,
h <- h - alpha (h.d) d, at residual_stream_post_layer: the layer's write
folded into the hyper-connection streams, before the next layer reads
Engram. Every stream is projected, so the stream mean the directions are
derived on is projected too.

Unset, the model has no steering module and the forward is unchanged.
Set, each layer's write is folded explicitly and the next layer takes the
folded streams, as an Engram layer does. The direction stack (zero rows
for unsteered layers) and alpha are buffers, so a file's contents never
change the traced graph, and the WEIGHTLESS_STEER_* variables are vLLM
env variables and so part of the compile cache key.

The reader is fail-closed: another mode, spec version, rank or hook
point; a direction for layer 0, outside the model, of another width, not
finite or not unit norm; a tensor that is not a direction; a layer list
that disagrees with the tensor names; or bytes past the last tensor stop
the boot. `python -m vllm.models.deepseek_v4_1.glp FILE` checks a file
without serving.

Reworked for spark-ds41f (christopherowen/spark-ds41f#401) from the
pending-FFN-write hotfix: steering moves to the folded residual that the
1017 GLP-39 file declares and was derived at, is absent rather than
zero-valued when off, and the .pt format, the global fallback vector and
the hook override are gone.
